{number: 167}
{title: Surely Goodness and Mercy}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [C] mind of peace and rest is mine,
A [F] table rich and [C] free;
With holy oil my head is crowned,
My [G7] cup runs over me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Surely [C] goodness and mercy shall [F] follow me
All the [C] days of my [G7] life;
Surely [C] goodness and mercy shall [F] follow me
All the [C] days of my [G7] life;
And I shall [C] dwell in the house of the [F] Lord for-[C] ever,
And I shall feast at the table spread for [G7] me;
Surely [C] goodness and mercy shall [F] follow me
All the [C] days, all the [G7] days of my [C] life.
{end_of_chorus}
